# Everything here is generated (regenerable via build/render/plot). Not tracked;
# the dated pre-build JSON is reproducible from the committed cache + registry.
*
!.gitignore
# The interned-id collision measured on the job 4901 partial (deleted after the build)
# and on the served KG 3.0 store (lane N, 2026-10-15): the evidence the fix and the
# release note cite, reproducible only against those two stores, so both are tracked.
!interned_id_collision_4901.json
!interned_id_collision_served.json
# The extended CSV endpoint gate (label check) run on the job 4901 partial, 2026-10-15.
!csv_endpoint_gate_labels_4901.json
# The bacterial tail's generation profile (lane S, job 4974, 2026-10-15) and the CSV
# endpoint gate over its 47 directories: the 19 GB of CSV they were read from is
# reclaimed before the 4.0 build and the serial run's telemetry with it, so neither is
# reproducible afterwards. The profile also carries the per-task seconds the full-array
# projection charged, which is the only surviving record of the job 4901 fold.
!bacterial_generation_profile_bacterial-tail.json
!bacterial_generation_csv_endpoint_gate.json
# The measured gene identifier vocabulary of the served stores is the evidence a
# schema-change record cites (P1, 2026-10-15); it is reproducible only against the
# served dev stores, so these two files are tracked.
!gene_id_namespace_vocabulary.md
!gene_id_namespace_vocabulary.json
# The attribution of the job 4901 partial's dangling PerturbationMemberOf rows (lane H,
# 2026-10-15) is evidence the KG 4.0 build decision cites; reproducible only against
# that partial's CSVs on /db, so the file is tracked.
!dangling_perturbation_rows_4901.json
# The environment-response identity outcomes (lane W, 2026-10-15): the bracketing
# duplicate counts the yeastphenome `expected_duplicated_pairs` constant and
# [[torchcell.verification.environment-response-identity]] cite, measured against the dev
# stores the KG 4.0 rebuild replaces, plus the field classification the note's table is.
!environment_response_identity_outcomes.json
!environment_response_identity_fields.json
# The media-name composition scan (lane X, 2026-10-15): the before-and-after yeastphenome
# token table, the L1 duplicate counts the `expected_duplicated_pairs` constant cites, and
# the cross-dataset scan of the dev stores. The store half is reproducible only against the
# PRE-fix dev stores that the KG 4.0 rebuild replaces, so the file is tracked.
!media_name_composition_scan.json
# The content-id collision scan (lanes Q and V, 2026-10-15): the whole-tree result over 176
# stores and the three per-store results for the datasets too large to scan with them
# (dmf_costanzo2016, dmi_costanzo2016, env_chemgen_hoepfner2014). Reproducible only against
# the PRE-fix dev stores the KG 4.0 rebuild replaces, so they are tracked -- the files were
# committed without this exception, which left them tracked and ignored at the same time, so
# a regenerated one would not be picked up by `git add`.
!content_id_collision_scan.json
!content_id_collision_scan_*.json
# The pre-build verification of the integrated branch (lane P, 2026-10-15): the nine stores
# built from it and the CSV endpoint gate over their generated directories. Same reason, and
# the same missing exception.
!prebuild_verify_stores.json
!prebuild_verify_csv_endpoint_gate.json
